[~accountid:60a8d304391e56006ec8d8fb] if you are talking about the manual verification we send an event from the BE: {{BUSINESS_MANUAL_VERIFICATION_ACCEPTED}}

Sending it from the FE means it will be re-sent on every page reload, once we don’t have a page that is shown only once for the user, so for this even the BE is the correct way.

Event on the FE are usually for tracking the customer usage, for example, tracking how many times they tried to click a button of a new functionality (eg: Add Agent). It does not mean that they are actually adding the agents, but we are getting data about how interested they are in the future, and, for example, later we can compare the interest with the actual quantity of new Agent that were created.

