Normally, we should confirm the VAT registration status of our partner, especially in circumstances where we generate invoices in their name. Going forward, due to the requirements under the DAC7, we must validate VAT ID of our partners, so that should somewhat alleviate this issue, albeit the non-registration would not be in the scope. 

 [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] [~accountid:61641a302f6aed0068fb7b50]  based on a quick check, I couldn’t find from Bolt Food T&Cs for couriers in PL the requirement for the couriers to notify us of the VAT status change (unlike some other countries, e.g. PT where: “_It is the responsibility of the Courier to ensure Bolt has up-to-date billing information, such as the Courier’s VAT status, NIF, name and address. In respect of the Courier’s VAT status, it is required that the Courier is registered for VAT under the normal regime, without applying any VAT exemption regimes. For the sake of clarity, Bolt cannot be held liable for any consequences deriving from the issue of invoices based on information provided by the Courier /.../)._ That said, the indemnification clauses seem to be sufficiently broad to cover any claims for incorrect invoices. 

Subject to confirmation from [~accountid:61641a302f6aed0068fb7b50] , my proposal is as follows: 

# "VAT %" denotes the applicable VAT rate. In case of tab 1 in the file, 0% is a reverse VAT charge. 

{color:#ff991f}_///DO WE NEED TO INCLUE EXPLANATION REGARDING REVERSE CHARGE VAT?///  -_ {color}{color:#0747a6}_If the fleet is not VAT registered, they shouldn’t normally be concerned with reverse charge. It’s technically not subject to the 0% rate but the taxpayer is merely not within the scope of VAT. But there are indeed a couple of invoices in the “VAT-registered” period to Bolt._ {color}

{color:#0747a6}_I would say: "VAT %" denotes the applicable VAT, including the absence of VAT for non-VAT registered persons (out of scope of VAT). In case of tab 1, 0% denotes services provided by a non-VAT registered person (out of scope of VAT) or otherwise intra-EU B2B services provided by the person (reverse charge by the customer)._  {color}


In a tab 2 VAT % is a applicable VAT charge.{color:#ff991f} _///I think we may need to explain that the fleet company requested VAT to be charged on some of these invoices and then decided to revoke it. WDYT?/// -_ {color}{color:#0747a6}_I think we should, assuming we have documentation in file confirming this correspondence?_ {color}

